  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA distributed value fell 5.6% over 30D:</strong> On-chain RWA distributed value at $15.00B (5.6% lower over 30D) hints that tokenized asset growth paused or reversed\u2014more consistent with risk-off allocation or redemptions than a pure news cycle. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/10/07/tether-tapped-by-kazakhstan-s-central-bank-to-explore-stablecoin-and-tokenization\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tether tapped by Kazakhstan\u2019s central bank to explore stablecoin and tokenization</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Tokenized U.S. Treasuries remain the institutional bridge into RWAs:</strong> adoption is strongest where products plug into cash management, collateral, and liquidity workflows. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/converge/tradfi-and-fintech/ondo-unveils-private-market-notes-ahead-of-first-ai-offering\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ondo Unveils Private-Market Notes Ahead of First AI Offering</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>Institutional commitments are still a leading share signal:</strong> Bank and asset-manager distribution deals often shift platform and network leadership before headline RWA totals fully catch up. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/business/2026-10-07-moodys-sky-protocol-b3-rating-first-stablecoin-protocol-417931\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Moody\u2019s gives Sky Protocol B3 rating as institutional interest in USDS grows</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Clearer rules tend to unlock balance-sheet participation and collateral workflows even when aggregate on-chain totals reprice slowly. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-card-access-doesnt-match-global-demand-tangem-says?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Crypto card access doesn\u2019t match global demand, Tangem says</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
